│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exemplar_anchored_voice                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The earlier versions were rule-driven. They stacked long lists of banned words and        │
│                          │ patterns. The model mostly ignored the voice rules and still wrote fluent textbook        │
│                          │ explanations, especially in notes. The heavy casual and lowercase style also cost task    │
│                          │ score without fooling the detector.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version is example-driven instead. It gives a few short, original human-style        │
│                          │ samples on unrelated topics, one per kind of writing. The model is told to copy their     │
│                          │ rhythm and density, never their content. Models imitate concrete examples much more       │
│                          │ reliably than they follow abstract rules.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also adds a small generation procedure. The model picks one angle, opens with a        │
│                          │ reaction or the answer, gives one judgement call, and stops early. This avoids the        │
│                          │ full-coverage explainer structure that detectors key on.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Reasoning is capped at a two-line plan, and rewrites start immediately, to get rid of     │
│                          │ empty outputs. The task rules target the observed off-task failures:                      │
│                          │ - Answer within the asker's frame.                                                        │
│                          │ - Never fabricate or point out missing questions.                                         │
│                          │ - Rewrites keep all facts.                                                                │
