│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hard_thinking_cap_with_samples                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The sample-based prompt is the only one that produced a passing output, but 8 of 25 tasks │
│                          │ came back empty. Each empty one used the whole 4096-token budget on reasoning, which also │
│                          │ pulled down the length and task scores.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The two earlier prompts had a firmer thinking limit and almost no empty outputs. This     │
│                          │ edit replaces the one-line budget with that stronger limit, with these additions:         │
│                          │ - It explicitly forbids checking the draft against the samples or the NEVER list while    │
│                          │ reasoning. Self-auditing against a long ban list is the likely cause of the runaway       │
│                          │ reasoning.                                                                                │
│                          │ - It says a missed rule is much cheaper than an empty answer.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also reframes the style rules as habits rather than a checklist the model must verify. │
│                          │ The last change adds one human-likeness cue: prefer concrete, specific everyday details   │
│                          │ over abstract explanation, since abstract explanation dominated the flagged outputs. That │
│                          │ is still bounded by the rule against invented facts.                                      │
