│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reddit_regular_minimal_think                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The context programs show two separate failure modes.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Empty outputs.** Long rule lists make the model plan and check every rule, so it     │
│                          │ burns its whole reasoning budget. The current program's big checklist produced 8 empty    │
│                          │ outputs.                                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. **AI flags.** Even with "casual" instructions, the outputs read as tidy explanatory    │
│                          │ prose: an ordered mechanism, balanced clauses and full textbook-style coverage. Swapping  │
│                          │ in a few casual words ("Honestly,") did not change that underlying shape.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The only pass came from a first-person, run-on, detail-driven rewrite. That suggests the  │
│                          │ detector rewards loose, conversational syntax more than vocabulary tweaks.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new approach does not ban patterns one by one. It gives the model one compact,        │
│                          │ imitable target voice: a forum regular typing on a phone. That voice brings loose         │
│                          │ punctuation, run-on clauses joined with "and"/"so", occasional "tbh/imo", sentences       │
│                          │ starting with "And" or "But", hedges, and an abrupt end. Ordered explanation is broken on │
│                          │ purpose: lead with the gut answer, mention the mechanism the way you'd half-remember it,  │
│                          │ and drift a bit.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Thinking is capped hard at one or two lines, and the prompt says outright that it         │
│                          │ contains no checklist to verify. Keeping the prompt short also cuts the urge to           │
│                          │ self-audit. Task-fidelity rules (no invented facts, length, emails, rewrites) are packed  │
│                          │ into a few lines so they still hold the task score.                                       │
