│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ no_think_exemplar_voice                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This prompt drops the long rulebooks used before and changes two things.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Shorter reasoning.**                                                                 │
│                          │    - It opens with Qwen's "/no_think" switch and a one-line plan instruction.             │
│                          │    - It gives only a few rules, so there is no checklist for the model to audit while it  │
│                          │ thinks. The long checklists seemed to cause the 4096-token overruns, which showed up as   │
│                          │ empty outputs, mostly on rewrites.                                                        │
│                          │    - Rewrites get their own procedure: rewrite straight through in the answer, top to     │
│                          │ bottom, without planning sentence by sentence.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Showing instead of listing.**                                                        │
│                          │    - Detectors flag fluent, even, explanatory prose, and abstract rules didn't move the   │
│                          │ model away from that.                                                                     │
│                          │    - So the prompt includes two short exemplar paragraphs I wrote on generic topics, not  │
│                          │ taken from any task. They show the target texture: an opinion up front, a lopsided        │
│                          │ structure, self-correction, and specific everyday framing.                                │
│                          │    - The model is told to match that texture, not to copy the content.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The remaining guidance targets the patterns seen in flagged outputs:                      │
│                          │ - definition-style openers                                                                │
│                          │ - tidy causal chains                                                                      │
│                          │ - "also/plus" enumerations of factors                                                     │
│                          │ - symmetric contrasts                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Task constraints (facts, length, email form, missing inputs) are kept to a few lines so   │
│                          │ task scores stay at 6 or above.                                                           │
