│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ short_prompt_no_wordcount                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The main loss is empty outputs: about a third of tasks spend the whole 4096-token budget  │
│                          │ reasoning. Two things seem to cause this. Long rule lists invite the model to check       │
│                          │ itself against each rule, and length targets invite word counting. The "/no_think" plus   │
│                          │ "plan in one line" combination also leaked a "Plan:" line into one output, which was then │
│                          │ judged off-task.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version does the following:                                                          │
│                          │ - Cuts the prompt down to a few compact paragraphs with fewer checkable rules.            │
│                          │ - Explicitly bans word counting and gives a paragraph-based length heuristic instead.     │
│                          │ - Bans drafting and tells the model to think in 2 or 3 sentences, then answer.            │
│                          │ - Forbids any plan or notes in the visible output.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The style guidance targets what Pangram flags: smooth explainer flow, factor-by-factor    │
│                          │ coverage, even sentence rhythm and tidy wrap-ups. It pushes toward:                       │
│                          │ - opinionated openings                                                                    │
│                          │ - one angle only                                                                          │
│                          │ - lopsided sentences                                                                      │
│                          │ - a mid-thought aside or self-correction                                                  │
│                          │ - slightly loose punctuation                                                              │
│                          │ - ending abruptly on a practical detail                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fact constraints and the email and rewrite format notes are kept, written briefly.    │
