│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hard_thinking_cap_and_no_selfcheck                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current prompt had 8 of 25 outputs come back empty. That is the biggest loss: those   │
│                          │ tasks fail on every metric. The likely cause is that the samples and the long NEVER list  │
│                          │ push the model to draft a version, compare it to the samples and audit it against the     │
│                          │ rules inside its reasoning.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit makes three changes:                                                            │
│                          │ - **Stronger thinking cap at the top.** It spells out that the model must not compare     │
│                          │ drafts to the samples and must not audit against the rules while thinking. It also says a │
│                          │ small rule slip costs less than an empty answer.                                          │
│                          │ - **Short reminder at the very end.** Recency matters for reasoning models, so the cap is │
│                          │ repeated just before "Output only the final text."                                        │
│                          │ - **Two style cues for the detector.** Pangram tends to flag smooth, evenly dense         │
│                          │ explanation. The new cues ask for a concrete everyday example in place of abstract        │
│                          │ mechanism, and for one small aside or tangent like the ones in the samples. They should   │
│                          │ lower AI scores without hurting task quality.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The samples stay because they produced the only pass so far.                              │
