│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ specific_not_performed_casual                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The feedback shows that performed casualness doesn't fool the detector. Openers like      │
│                          │ "yeah so", lowercase text and "imo/iirc" still scored 82-95. What gets flagged is the     │
│                          │ underlying shape of AI explanation: a smooth mechanism walkthrough, generic category      │
│                          │ words ("a beat, a horn riff, a vocal lick..."), connective phrases like "that's why" and  │
│                          │ "think of it like", and tidy cohesion. The only pass was a plain, concrete retelling.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit changes the style guidance in four ways:                                        │
│                          │ - **Specifics over categories:** less predictable word choice, one concrete example       │
│                          │ rather than a list, and replies aimed at the asker's own situation.                       │
│                          │ - **Mixed punctuation:** some questions and parentheses.                                  │
│                          │ - **Loose links between sentences:** less "so/because" glue, with jumps between points.   │
│                          │ - **Slang dialled back:** the forced openers and shorthand are removed.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also bans the newly observed tells: "basically", "think of it like", "the big          │
│                          │ difference is", "that's why", "under the hood", "first off".                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Two task fixes:                                                                           │
│                          │ - The off-task post invented experience ("I've been buying cars for years"), so the       │
│                          │ no-invented-credentials rule is now stricter.                                             │
│                          │ - The email answer added odd "facts", so I added a rule against stating anything you      │
│                          │ aren't sure of.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The thinking limit stays tight, and rewrites get an explicit instruction to start writing │
│                          │ immediately.                                                                              │
