                         Patch Metadata - Gen 13/16 - Novelty: 1/1 - Resample: 1/2 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fixed_think_template_voice_cards                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The prompt now has three blocks in a fixed order.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **A fill-in thinking template.** The model's reasoning is reduced to one line (`kind / │
│                          │ length / my take`) followed by "Go". It is told that rules are not to be checked in       │
│                          │ thinking and that rewrites need no thinking at all. This targets the empty outputs that   │
│                          │ came from over-planning rewrites and emails, and from re-reading rules.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **One compact voice persona.** The model writes as someone who half-remembers the      │
│                          │ topic, and explanations are framed as how the writer understands it. This shift comes     │
│                          │ from the failures: clean, impersonal explanatory prose kept getting flagged, while the    │
│                          │ one first-person, concrete narrative passed. The persona allows mild run-ons, uneven      │
│                          │ paragraphs, a self-correction and an abrupt ending. It drops the long list of forbidden   │
│                          │ phrases, which invites rule-checking.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Short per-kind cards.** Separate cards cover answer/note, post, email and rewrite.   │
│                          │ The model only needs the relevant card, so it doesn't re-reason about all the rules.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The length mapping to paragraph counts is kept, so the model never counts words.          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
