                         Patch Metadata - Gen 14/16 - Novelty: 1/1 - Resample: 1/2 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ opinionated_regular_low_think                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ **What the current prompt controls.** Its main settings are:                              │
│                          │ - the thinking cap (5 lines);                                                             │
│                          │ - the opener style, which recommended "Honestly" and "Short answer";                      │
│                          │ - a banned-word list;                                                                     │
│                          │ - the formatting bans;                                                                    │
│                          │ - the task rules;                                                                         │
│                          │ - the default length (120 to 250 words).                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **What the failures show.**                                                               │
│                          │ - Task score and length were fine, but every output was flagged as AI.                    │
│                          │ - The recommended openers showed up in most flagged texts ("Short answer:", "Honestly,"), │
│                          │ and those openers are detector bait.                                                      │
│                          │ - The first prior program's lowercase-messy style also failed. Sloppy grammar alone does  │
│                          │ not fool the detector.                                                                    │
│                          │ - The real issue is the genre. Outputs read as tidy explainers: textbook mechanism, "your │
│                          │ brain / your body" framing, "so the X", "which is why".                                   │
│                          │ - The only text that passed was flat, concrete narration with low explanatory             │
│                          │ scaffolding.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **New configuration.**                                                                    │
│                          │ 1. Keep a hard 3-line thinking cap. No drafting or counting, and rewrites start at once.  │
│                          │ Few empty outputs depend on this.                                                         │
│                          │ 2. Swap the persona from "helpful explainer" to "opinionated regular". This writer:       │
│                          │    - makes claims flatly, without walking the reader through them;                        │
│                          │    - uses concrete, everyday, slightly unusual words and idioms;                          │
│                          │    - adds one aside or tangent;                                                           │
│                          │    - shows mild attitude.                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Ban the explainer connective tissue explicitly: "which is why", "that's why", "so      │
│                          │ basically", "the thing is", "your brain", "the body", and analogy setups like "think of   │
│                          │ it like".                                                                                 │
│                          │ 4. Ban the formula openers I used to recommend, and ban openers built on a filler         │
│                          │ interjection.                                                                             │
│                          │ 5. Ask for declarative short-to-medium sentences with low hedging density: at most one    │
│                          │ hedge.                                                                                    │
│                          │ 6. Prefer one specific concrete example over a general explanation, without inventing     │
│                          │ facts.                                                                                    │
│                          │ 7. Tighten the default length band to 110 to 200 words.                                   │
│                          │ 8. Keep rewrites close to the source's flat narrative style, since that is what passed.   │
