│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ habits_not_checklist_one_line_plan                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Two problems hurt the score at once. Four outputs were empty, and nearly everything else  │
│                          │ was flagged as AI or marked off-task.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Empty outputs.** These most likely come from the model treating the long rule list as a │
│                          │ checklist. It audits its draft against every rule during reasoning and runs out of        │
│                          │ budget. The fix:                                                                          │
│                          │ - Cut the plan to one line.                                                               │
│                          │ - Say outright that the rules are habits, not a checklist.                                │
│                          │ - Forbid re-checking.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **AI flags.** The flagged texts are tidy explainers: background first, then the           │
│                          │ mechanism, then a summary. Pangram keys on that explanatory density and on even,          │
│                          │ low-surprise prose. I'm replacing the micro-rules (one question, one parenthetical, and   │
│                          │ so on) with a simpler, more generative stance:                                            │
│                          │ - Lead with your own take on the asker's specific situation.                              │
│                          │ - Allow one sideways aside, like a pet peeve or a common misconception.                   │
│                          │ - Include one blunt short sentence.                                                       │
│                          │ - Use concrete nouns from their situation.                                                │
│                          │ - Explicitly avoid textbook mechanism exposition.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Off-task answers.** "Give the gist, leave stuff out" sometimes produced vague text. I'm │
│                          │ adding an explicit rule that the answer must still contain the actual reason or solution  │
│                          │ the asker needs, stated plainly early on.                                                 │
